
# LanCache-NG (https://github.com/wiki-mod/lancache-ng)
# SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later
# Git ignore patterns for build artifacts, secrets, and generated files

# Cache data - never commit
data/
/cache/
/kea/
/nats/
/nats-conf/
/pdns-standard/
/pdns-ssl/
/pdns-filter-state/

# Generated certificates (keep only the CA template, not issued certs)
certs/*.crt
certs/*.key
certs/*.pem
!certs/.gitkeep

# Generated BIND9 keys (auto-created at container startup)
services/dns/keys/

# Generated Kea secrets (auto-created at container startup)
services/dhcp/keys/

# Environment files with secrets (root-level only)
/.env
/.env.dev
/.env.prod
deploy/prod/.env.local

# config/*.env files are committed (no secrets, just operational config)

# Claude Code project settings
.claude/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Rust build artifacts
services/ui/target/
services/dns/nats-subscriber/target/
# Issue #1415: found missing while running a local, non-authoritative
# `cargo check`/`test`/`clippy` sanity pass against services/watchdog's
# Rust crate (the real, CI-authoritative validation still runs inside the
# build-tools container per AG-VAL-016) -- this entry was simply never
# added when watchdog gained its own Cargo.toml.
services/watchdog/target/
# Issue #871: added when services/warmer (renamed services/cachehamster
# during its infra integration, same issue) gained its own Cargo.toml,
# same gap #1415's comment above already describes for watchdog -- added
# immediately this time rather than discovered missing later, after this
# session's own local cargo build/test/clippy/fmt sanity pass (real
# commands/output in this PR's own body) against services/warmer.
services/cachehamster/target/

# Editor
*.swp
*.swo
.idea/
.vscode/
